prompt:
{
  "public_instructions": "You translate natural-language access-control requirements into Cedar policies using the supplied schema. Cedar denies by default. An applicable forbid overrides every permit. Guard optional attributes with has before reading them. Preserve the schema's entity, set, and attribute types. Use only the supplied task information. Do not use tools, files, search, additional model calls, or external feedback. Produce a single final answer as a JSON object with exactly one field, policy, whose value is the complete Cedar policy text. Do not include explanations or Markdown fences.
",
  "harness": {
    "instruction_blocks": [
      "Translate the access-control requirements into a complete Cedar policy set. Identify each action, eligible principal, resource type, required condition, prohibition, and exception. Use only entity types, attributes, actions, and representations supported by the schema. Implement the stated permissions and restrictions together.",
      "Before answering, check the policy mentally for both unauthorized permissions and missing required permissions. Keep distinct action rules separate when their conditions differ. Apply exceptions only to the restriction they qualify. Return one final policy set."
    ],
    "input_order": [
      "requirements",
      "schema"
    ],
    "checklist": [
      "Every required action is covered.",
      "Role, ownership, membership, and context conditions follow the requirements.",
      "Prohibitions and exceptions compose correctly.",
      "Optional attribute reads are guarded and Cedar syntax is valid."
    ]
  },
  "requirements": "The system manages course modules and gradebook entries in a learning-management system.

The people involved are instructors of record, teaching assistants, learners, and coordinators. One person may hold both the instructor of record and teaching assistant roles at the same time.

The resources are modules and grade entries. Every module records its course, instructor of record, roster, prerequisite level, release time, locked setting, and status.

Every grade entry records its learner, module, who posted it, and its status.

Each requester carries their completed level.

Each request carries the current time, whether it is on the institution network, and the preview window.

An instructor of record or teaching assistant may enter a grade only while the grade entry is in draft status.

An instructor of record or teaching assistant must not enter a grade when the grade entry is not in draft status.

A person who is neither an instructor of record nor a teaching assistant must not enter a grade.

When the grade entry is in draft status, an instructor of record or teaching assistant may enter the grade if no other rule blocks the request.

A request by an instructor of record to enter a draft grade entry that trips no prohibition above must be able to succeed.",
  "schema": "entity Role enum ["InstructorOfRecord", "TeachingAssistant", "Learner", "Coordinator"];

entity Person {
    roles: Set<Role>,
    completedLevel: Long,
};

entity Course;

entity Module {
    course: Course,
    instructorOfRecord: Person,
    roster: Set<Person>,
    prerequisiteLevel: Long,
    releaseTime: datetime,
    locked: Bool,
    status: String,
};

entity GradeEntry {
    learner: Person,
    module: Module,
    postedBy: Person,
    status: String,
};

action enterGrade appliesTo {
    principal: [Person],
    resource: [GradeEntry],
    context: {
        currentTime: datetime,
        onInstitutionNetwork: Bool,
        previewWindow: { start: datetime, end: datetime },
    },
};
"
}
